    {
      "id": "claim_d82f88f3daa04efeacd6ef5092f8d56e",
      "statement": "Every agent/reviewer run trigger (Slack, Linear, GitHub, dashboard, scheduler) routes through a single durable dispatch contract, openswe/dispatch.py:dispatch_agent_run, which selects the graph via assistant_id ('agent' or 'reviewer') and treats source as metadata/logging only.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/dispatch.py#L415-L467",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:28afdd7a53e23a471f0d684899ac0379927fe003ea4786f006fddd22a53cc2f0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_45387ab772f3437e9c3a2030f69732d5",
      "statement": "The dispatch contract defaults to multitask_strategy='interrupt' (a follow-up halts and resumes the active run with full history plus the new message), durability='async' checkpointing before each step written while the next step runs, resumable stream_resumable plus v3 protocol markers so the dashboard can attach to and observe runs it did not itself start. Background work may explicitly choose another multitask strategy such as 'enqueue'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/dispatch.py#L1-L27",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b089ea59a45f0c547ce3888dd68945ebf8ab2807ad74643a752299105aa6a940:"
